From 2048e00b06c090cfe62a95810bfd18963ab8d088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:49:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Options of BoomerAMG

The HypreBoomerAMG preconditioner (and linear solver) accepts the options
StrengthThreshold, CoarseningType, AggressiveCoarseningLevels,
InterpolationType, RelaxationType, RelaxationSweeps, CycleType,
NumberOfCycles and MaximumNumberOfLevels (values of hypre).
`HypreBoomerAMG::SetOperator` only keeps some options of hypre: the
settings, including the systems options, are applied again after each
SetOperator (ConfiguredHypreBoomerAMG, replacing SystemHypreBoomerAMG).

FixedPointSolver: the residual is profiled as for the Newton solver, and
the actions associated with new estimates are only called if any.

FixedPointSolverTest: two cycles of BoomerAMG per iteration reduce the
number of iterations of the fixed point (the setting survives the setup
of the elastic operator).
---
 src/FixedPointSolver.cxx       |   8 ++
 src/LinearSolverFactory.cxx    | 197 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 tests/FixedPointSolverTest.cxx |  26 +++++
 3 files changed, 166 insertions(+), 65 deletions(-)

